  "summary": "Parkes Observatory in central-west New South Wales hosts a 64-metre radio telescope, officially opened on 31 October 1961 by the Governor-General. In July 1969 it supplied the signals behind most of the international television broadcast of the Apollo 11 moonwalk, taking over from Honeysuckle Creek partway through.",
